# Frontend Quality

- Inspect and preserve the existing design system, route behavior, data flow,
  and interaction contracts unless change is explicit.
- Choose one coherent visual thesis; avoid generic gradient, glass, card-grid,
  pill-everything, oversized-empty-hero, and decorative-reveal defaults.
- Implement loading, empty, error, success, disabled, focus, overflow, and
  reduced-motion states where applicable.
- Use semantic elements, labels, keyboard operation, visible focus, non-color
  status cues, practical touch targets, and WCAG AA contrast.
- Prevent layout shift, clipping, horizontal overflow, focus loss, and
  inaccessible custom controls.
- Validate at 320, 375, 768, 1280, and 1440 pixel widths plus a short laptop
  height when rendering tools are available.
- Preserve secrets and privileged operations behind server-side boundaries.
